{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3398": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer / Instructor of Athletic Training",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Assistant Athletic Trainer / Instructor of Athletic Training The University of Evansville Department of Athletics is seeking a dedicated, student-centered, and collaborative athletic training professional to join our Sports Medicine team. This position will assist the Associate Athletic Director for Sports Medicine in providing comprehensive healthcare services for University student-athletes while also supporting the School of Health Sciences Athletic Training Program through classroom instruction and clinical education. The successful candidate will serve as the primary athletic trainer for Women's Volleyball and may be assigned additional sport coverage as determined by the Associate Athletic Director for Sports Medicine. This position combines clinical athletic training responsibilities with teaching and clinical supervision duties, providing a unique opportunity to contribute to both student-athlete health and athletic training education. Key Responsibilities The Assistant Athletic Trainer / Instructor will balance athletic training services, educational responsibilities, and administrative duties. Primary responsibilities include: Athletic Training & Sports Medicine Provide prevention, evaluation, treatment, and rehabilitation of athletic injuries and illnesses for assigned student-athletes. Develop and implement injury prevention and rehabilitation programs in collaboration with the Sports Medicine team. Deliver healthcare education and counseling to student-athletes. Communicate effectively with student-athletes, physicians, coaching staff, and parents, when appropriate, regarding injury status and treatment plans. Coordinate and provide medical coverage for practices, competitions, and team travel. Collaborate with physicians and allied healthcare professionals to ensure comprehensive care for student-athletes. Maintain accurate electronic medical records and injury documentation. Assist with insurance claim processing and related administrative functions. Support scheduling and coordination of medical coverage for home and away athletic events. Teaching & Clinical Education Provide instruction within the School of Health Sciences Athletic Training Program. Serve as a clinical preceptor and mentor for Athletic Training students. Supervise, educate, and evaluate Athletic Training students and athletic training interns. Assist with recruitment and retention efforts for the Athletic Training Program. Promote professional development and evidence-based practice among students. Administrative Responsibilities Maintain accurate records related to athletic training services, student clinical experiences, and insurance processing. Ensure compliance with University, NCAA, BOC, state licensure, and accreditation requirements. Participate in departmental meetings, professional development activities, and other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Master's degree in Athletic Training, Exercise Science, Health Sciences, or a closely related field. Board of Certification (BOC) certification. Indiana Athletic Trainer License or eligibility for licensure. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with student-athletes, students, faculty, coaches, healthcare providers, and parents. Ability to perform the physical requirements of the position, including lifting and carrying equipment and supplies. Ability to work a flexible schedule that includes evenings, weekends, holidays, and team travel. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with softball or similar overhead-throwing sports. Previous collegiate athletic training experience. Teaching experience in higher education. Experience serving as a clinical preceptor for athletic training students. Experience with athletic insurance claims processing and documentation systems. Demonstrated commitment to student learning and mentorship. Working Conditions This position requires regular evening and weekend work, extensive athletic event coverage, and team travel. The successful candidate will function in both clinical and academic environments and will serve as an instructor and clinical supervisor within the Athletic Training Program. Why Join the University of Evansville? The University of Evansville offers a collaborative environment where athletic healthcare professionals play a critical role in both student-athlete success and the education of future athletic trainers. This position provides the opportunity to impact student-athlete wellness while contributing to an accredited academic program dedicated to preparing the next generation of healthcare professionals. How to Apply Interested candidates should complete the online application via the University of Evansville’s employment portal: http://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employmentApp.cfm The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3393": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President for Institutional Research and Effectiveness",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Assistant Vice President for Institutional Research and Effectiveness The University of Evansville invites applications for the position of Assistant Vice President for Institutional Research and Effectiveness. This full-time leadership position provides strategic direction for the University's institutional research, assessment, and data analytics initiatives. Reporting to senior leadership, the Assistant Vice President serves as the University's primary resource for data-informed decision-making and institutional effectiveness. The successful candidate will lead efforts related to data collection, analysis, reporting, accreditation support, and strategic planning while ensuring the integrity, accessibility, and responsible use of institutional data across the University. Key Responsibilities The Assistant Vice President for Institutional Research and Effectiveness provides leadership for institutional research, data governance, assessment activities, and strategic reporting. Institutional Research & Analytics Lead and manage the Office of Institutional Research and Effectiveness, including supervision of institutional research staff and data analysts. Oversee the collection, analysis, interpretation, and dissemination of institutional data for internal and external stakeholders. Develop meaningful analyses that support strategic planning, policy development, enrollment management, student success initiatives, and institutional effectiveness efforts. Serve as a trusted advisor to University leadership by providing data-informed insights and recommendations. Strategic Planning & Institutional Effectiveness Support institutional planning processes through research, assessment, benchmarking, and performance analysis. Partner with academic and administrative leaders to establish, monitor, and evaluate key performance indicators. Develop procedures and frameworks that promote continuous improvement across the institution. Facilitate evidence-based decision-making throughout the University. Reporting & Compliance Coordinate and complete all required external reporting, including submissions to: Integrated Postsecondary Education Data System (IPEDS) State agencies Accrediting organizations Higher education consortia and surveys Ensure accuracy, consistency, and timeliness of all institutional reporting activities. Maintain comprehensive documentation of reporting methodologies and data definitions. Accreditation & Assessment Lead and support accreditation efforts by providing institutional data, assessment results, and evidence-based analyses. Collaborate with campus stakeholders to evaluate institutional outcomes and effectiveness measures. Assist academic and administrative units with assessment planning, implementation, and reporting. Support the University's commitment to continuous quality improvement and accountability. Data Management & Visualization Develop and maintain dashboards, reports, and data visualization tools that provide accessible and actionable institutional information. Promote transparency through the creation of user-friendly reporting resources and self-service data tools. Identify opportunities to improve institutional data infrastructure and reporting capabilities. Support campus stakeholders through training and consultation on data interpretation and utilization. Collaboration & Leadership Partner with Information Technology, Enrollment Management, Academic Affairs, Student Affairs, Fiscal Affairs, and other University departments to ensure data alignment and consistency. Foster a culture of assessment, accountability, and evidence-based decision-making. Serve on institutional committees and work groups as appropriate. Represent the University in professional organizations and external collaborations related to institutional research and effectiveness. Data Governance & Compliance Ensure compliance with federal, state, and institutional regulations related to data privacy and security, including FERPA requirements. Promote ethical research practices and responsible stewardship of institutional data. Develop and maintain data governance standards, policies, and procedures. Required Qualifications Master's degree in Education, Statistics, Data Science, Public Policy, Higher Education, Research Methodology, or a related field. Minimum of seven years of progressively responsible experience in institutional research, assessment, data analytics, or a related area within higher education. Demonstrated leadership and supervisory experience. Expertise with data management tools, statistical software, and analytics platforms such as SQL, SPSS, SAS, R, Tableau, Power BI, or similar systems. Strong understanding of higher education reporting requirements, accountability measures, and institutional effectiveness practices. Excellent analytical, communication, presentation, and project management skills. Ability to communicate complex data and findings to both technical and non-technical audiences. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in a related field. Experience supporting regional accreditation processes and self-study efforts. Familiarity with higher education enterprise systems and student information systems. Experience developing institutional dashboards and data visualization solutions. Knowledge of enrollment, retention, graduation, and student success analytics. Experience advancing data governance and institutional effectiveness initiatives. Working Environment This position works closely with senior leadership and collaborates extensively with academic and administrative units across the University. The successful candidate will lead complex projects, oversee multiple reporting deadlines, and provide strategic guidance on matters related to institutional performance, assessment, and data-informed decision-making. Why Join the University of Evansville? The University of Evansville is committed to academic excellence, student success, and continuous improvement. The Assistant Vice President for Institutional Research and Effectiveness plays a critical leadership role in advancing these priorities by providing the data, analysis, and strategic insights that guide institutional planning and decision-making. This position offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact on the University's future through leadership in research, assessment, and institutional effectiveness. How to Apply Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume/CV, and contact information for three professional references. In addition, candidates should complete the online application through the University of Evansville employment portal: http://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employmentApp.cfm Legal Statement The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Any form of harassment undermines the mission of the University and negatively impacts the University community as a whole. The University of Evansville participates in the E-Verify program. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3399": {
      "title": "Athletics Annual Giving Officer",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Athletics Annual Giving Officer The University of Evansville Athletics Department invites applications for a strategic and relationship-driven Athletics Annual Giving Officer. Reporting directly to the Director of Athletic Development, this role plays a pivotal part in growing philanthropic support for our Purple Aces student-athletes and programs. You will lead the charge on unrestricted and sport-specific fundraising appeals, manage a dedicated donor portfolio, and build a vibrant culture of philanthropy across our entire athletics community. Key Responsibilities Case for Support: Craft and communicate compelling narratives articulating the impact of unrestricted athletics giving, developing high-impact marketing materials and presentations. Annual Unrestricted Appeals: Plan and execute comprehensive fundraising campaigns for the unrestricted athletics fund, including spearheading outreach for Pep and Vim week (the University's annual giving week) across multi-channel platforms (email, direct mail, social, and events). Sport-Specific Giving: Serve as the primary point of contact for sports-specific annual funds, working directly with coaches, athletics staff, and Major Gift Officers to execute Support Your Sport week and meet operational funding goals. Pipeline & Leadership Giving: Manage a portfolio of up to 75 athletics prospects and donors, driving cultivation, solicitation, and stewardship for gifts ranging from $1,000 to $49,000 to build the major gift pipeline. Donor Acquisition & Retention: Focus on boosting overall donor participation, retention, upgrades, and stewardship for the Purple Aces Club and sport-specific funds. Calendar & Compliance: Manage the comprehensive Athletics Annual Fund Calendar, ensuring timely outreach and that all donor benefits are accurately delivered. Required Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree required, preferably in business, marketing, sports management, or a related field. Experience: Minimum of 3 years of professional experience in fundraising, alumni relations, or related fields (preferably in athletics or higher education). Technical Proficiency: Demonstrated experience working with CRM software and fundraising databases. Core Skills: Exceptional communication, relationship-building, and project management capabilities, with a proven knack for donor engagement and multi-channel fundraising appeals. Availability & Environment: Flexibility to travel as needed for athletics events and engage in occasional evening and weekend work during peak fundraising periods and games. Why Join UE Athletics? At the University of Evansville, philanthropy is the fuel that powers championship-level experiences for our student-athletes. As our Athletics Annual Giving Officer, you will work in a collaborative, high-energy Division I environment where your daily creativity and donor outreach directly translate into enhanced resources, facility upgrades, and programmatic success for the Purple Aces. How to Apply Interested candidates should complete the online application via the University of Evansville’s employment portal: http://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employmentApp.cfm The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, and all federally protected groups/classes. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3375": {
      "title": "Coordinator for Fitness Center and Intramural Sports",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Coordinator for Fitness Center and Intramural Sports The University of Evansville (UE) Student Affairs division is seeking an energetic, organized, and student-focused Coordinator for Fitness Center and Intramural Sports. This is a full-time university administrator role that plays a vital part in campus life, promoting health, wellness, and community through comprehensive recreational programming. As the Coordinator, you will help manage our Student Fitness Center: featuring free weights, cardio equipment, court spaces, an indoor track, a swimming pool, and field spaces, while leading a robust intramural sports schedule. If you are passionate about collegiate recreation, student leadership development, and active campus engagement, we want to hear from you. Key Responsibilities The Coordinator balances facility management with active student programming and staff development. Your main duties will include: Intramural Program Management: Coordinate a large-scale, engaging intramural sports program consisting of 30+ events annually for students, faculty, and staff. Student Staff Leadership: Recruit, train, and supervise a large team of student employees, including sports officials, game supervisors, and facility lifeguards. Facility Operations: Support the daily operation and management of the Student Fitness Center in partnership with the Director. Health & Fitness Programming: Assist with general wellness programming, fitness challenges, and educational health initiatives for the campus community. Collaborative Partnerships: Partner with the Director to hire and supervise fitness center student staff, and collaborate closely with the campus Esports program on fitness-related initiatives and intramural coordination. University Service: Represent the department and serve on various university committees as needed. Required Qualifications Education: A Bachelor’s Degree is required Experience: Professional experience in recreational sports management, preferably within a collegiate setting. Leadership Skills: Demonstrated ability to recruit, mentor, and supervise student staff in a fast-paced environment. Availability: Due to the nature of student recreation, this position requires evenings and flexible day hours to support programs and events. Why Join the UE Student Affairs Team? At the University of Evansville, campus recreation is central to student wellness, retention, and community building. As part of our Student Affairs team, you will work in an energetic, supportive environment where your leadership directly impacts student life. You will have the autonomy to shape exciting intramural leagues, mentor student workers, and foster a lifelong culture of health on campus. How to Apply Interested candidates should complete the online application via the University of Evansville’s employment portal: http://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employmentApp.cfm The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3397": {
      "title": "Director, Emily M. Young Mental Health Clinic",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Director, Emily M. Young Mental Health Clinic The University of Evansville is seeking a strategic, compassionate, and experienced healthcare leader to serve as the Clinic Director for the Emily M. Young Mental Health Clinic. This leadership position oversees all administrative and operational activities for the clinic, ensuring the delivery of high-quality, ethical, and evidence-based psychological services while maintaining strict compliance with applicable laws, regulations, and professional standards. The Clinic Director acts as the overall supervisor for the facility, managing the daily operations of the Clinic Coordinator, Physician Assistant, and support staff. (Note: If the successful candidate is a licensed mental health practitioner, then this role also assumes a direct clinical caseload, student supervision, and teaching responsibilities.) Responsibilities Include: Administrative Leadership Oversee the daily operations of the clinic. Develop and implement policies and procedures that promote efficient and effective operations. Ensure compliance with federal, state, and local regulations, accreditation standards, and professional ethical guidelines. Participate in strategic planning, quality improvement initiatives, and program development. Monitor clinical productivity and operational performance. Manage the clinical’s operating budget, including revenue and expenses. Market the clinic’s services to the local community. Assist the Office of University Advancement with fundraising and grant applications. Directly supervise the Clinic Coordinator, including scheduling, administrative workflows, customer service, billing, provider credentialing, and front-office operations. Supervise work study and graduate assistants. Provide administrative supervision to the Physician Assistant (i.e., job performance and organizational responsibilities) as permitted by state law and within the Physician Assistant’s scope of practice, ensuring coordinated behavioral health services. Clinical supervision of the Physician Assistant will be provided by a licensed physician. Conduct annual performance evaluations, provide coaching, and support professional development for all clinic staff. Foster a collaborative, respectful, and patient-centered work environment. Monitor inventory of supplies and testing equipment and work with University departments to ensure the safety and comfort of the clinic. Complete University reports as requested. Provide hiring recommendations, onboarding, training, performance evaluations, coaching, scheduling, and disciplinary actions consistent with clinic policies. Quality Assurance Ensure the quality, effectiveness, and ethical delivery of clinical services provided. Develop and implement evidence-based protocols and clinical policies. Review and monitor clinical documentation for quality and regulatory compliance. Address patient concerns and resolve clinical issues. Develop patient outcome measures and monitor patient satisfaction. Implement quality improvement initiatives as appropriate. Ensure appropriate coordination of care with referring providers and community resources. Promote a culture of safety, confidentiality, and continuous improvement. Ensure compliance with HIPAA, OSHA, payer requirements, state licensing regulations, and University policies. Maintain accurate clinical records and documentation standards. Participate in incident review, risk management activities, and corrective action planning when necessary. If a licensed mental health practitioner, then: Maintain a clinical caseload as determined by clinic needs and task priorities. Provide consultation to trainees, staff, and other clinicians who need psychological treatment input regarding a patient. Manage clinical emergencies and provide clinical consultation to students and staff for suicide risk assessments and safety planning. Serve as an accessible clinical resource for students who require consultation regarding patient care, clinical decision-making, documentation, and professional conduct. Collaborate with academic leadership and faculty to address matters that affect clinical training and student progress. Provide direct clinical supervision to students. Teach (up to) one course per year. Review and address time-sensitive clinical matters to ensure continuity and safety of patient care during another practitioner’s absence. Make the necessary clinical decisions when other clinical staff are unavailable. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in healthcare administration, health services, social work, counseling, or a related field. Two years of progressively responsible administrative or management experience in healthcare, behavioral health, human services, or a comparable setting. Demonstrated experience managing or coordinating healthcare operations, including personnel, scheduling, workflow, policies and procedures, and resource allocation. Demonstrated ability to lead and supervise employees and work effectively with multidisciplinary professionals. Knowledge of confidentiality, privacy, compliance, and risk-management requirements applicable to healthcare or other confidential service environments. Strong organizational, communication, problem-solving, and decision-making skills. Preferred Qualifications Master’s or Doctorate degree in a relevant field. Three or more years of progressively responsible administrative or management experience in healthcare. Experience managing an outpatient healthcare or behavioral health clinic. Experience with budgeting, electronic health records, quality improvement, regulatory compliance, and healthcare reimbursement. Experience working in a university or academic clinical environment. Professional licensure in a mental health or related healthcare discipline is preferred but not required for this position. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Excellent leadership and supervisory abilities. Knowledge of outpatient behavioral health operations. Strong organizational and problem-solving skills. Effective written and verbal communication. Ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining high standards of patient care. Proficiency with electronic health records (EHR) and practice management software. Why Join the University of Evansville? At the University of Evansville, our clinics are vital pillars of both community wellness and student professional development. As Clinic Director, you will lead a dedicated team in a supportive academic environment, shaping the operational and clinical success of an essential university resource. How to Apply Interested candidates should complete the online application and submit their resume, cover letter, and any other application materials via the University of Evansville’s employment portal: http://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employmentApp.cfm The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, and all federally protected groups/classes. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3236": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant - Golf Coach",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Graduate Assistant - Golf Coach The University of Evansville, a proud member of the Missouri Valley Conference, is currently accepting applications for a Graduate Assistant position to support both the Men’s and Women’s Golf programs. This is an exciting opportunity for a passionate and knowledgeable individual to gain valuable coaching experience at the NCAA Division I level while pursuing a graduate degree. Position Summary: The Graduate Assistant – Golf Coach will assist with all aspects of the men’s and women’s golf programs, including but not limited to: Practice planning and preparation Scouting opponents Recruiting student-athletes Travel coordination Equipment management Administrative support and other duties as assigned by the head coach The successful candidate will demonstrate strong knowledge of golf fundamentals and NCAA rules, excellent communication skills, and the ability to engage effectively with student-athletes, staff, faculty, and the broader campus community. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required with a minimum 3.0 GPA Division I collegiate golf experience preferred CPR, First Aid, and AED certification (or ability to obtain) Valid driver’s license required Excellent written and verbal communication skills Understanding of and commitment to NCAA, Missouri Valley Conference, and University regulations and values Compensation: This Graduate Assistant position includes full tuition coverage for a master’s degree program at the University of Evansville. The University of Evansville offers a generous benefits package to eligible employees, including: Comprehensive Health, Vision, Dental, Group Life, Voluntary Life, and ancillary benefits. Access to our exclusive on-site medical clinic for those enrolled in our Health plan Excellent 403(b) retirement match and a Roth, up to 5% 100% Tuition Remission and Tuition Exchange programs for you, your spouse, and dependents Comprehensive paid holidays and vacation time with the option to purchase additional days Generous sick policy for peace of mind How to Apply: Interested candidates should submit a resume, cover letter, and references via the University of Evansville’s employment portal: http://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employmentApp.cfm The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Any form of harassment undermines the mission of the University and negatively impacts the University community as a whole. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3401": {
      "title": "Slate Operations Specialist",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Slate Operations Specialist The Slate Operations Specialist works closely with admission, marketing, and financial aid staff to support communication plans, data management, reporting, and recruitment initiatives. This role is ideal for an organized, detail-oriented professional who enjoys working with technology, data, and processes in a collaborative, fast-paced environment. The successful candidate will bring a foundation of professional experience and a willingness to develop expertise in Slate and enrollment operations. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree required. One to two years of experience in admissions, enrollment management, CRM administration, data management, marketing operations, customer relationship management, or a related field. Strong attention to detail and organizational skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to learn new technologies and systems quickly. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively as part of a team. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with CRM systems, databases, or data management processes. Experience in higher education admissions or enrollment management. Familiarity with Slate CRM or other enrollment management technologies. Experience creating reports, analyzing data, or supporting operational processes. Experience supporting communication campaigns, event management, or recruitment initiatives. Why Join the University of Evansville? The Office of Admission plays a critical role in advancing the University's enrollment goals and mission. The Slate Operations Specialist will contribute to undergraduate recruitment efforts through data management, communication support, and enrollment operations while gaining valuable experience in CRM administration, enrollment management, and higher education technology. How to Apply Interested candidates should complete the online application via the University of Evansville’s employment portal: http://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employmentApp.cfm The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3400": {
      "title": "Staff Accountant",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Staff Accountant The University of Evansville invites applications for the position of Staff Accountant. This full-time position is responsible for supporting the University's accounting operations through financial reporting, account reconciliations, grant accounting, fixed asset management, and various general accounting functions. The successful candidate will join a collaborative accounting team that supports faculty, staff, students, and administrative departments across the University. The Staff Accountant will play a key role in maintaining accurate financial records, ensuring compliance with accounting standards, and supporting sound financial stewardship of University resources. Key Responsibilities The Staff Accountant supports the Business and Finance Office through a variety of accounting and financial reporting functions. Financial Accounting & Reporting Record, monitor, and track capital assets and depreciation. Prepare, analyze, and process monthly journal entries. Reconcile general ledger accounts and bank statements. Assist in maintaining the accuracy and integrity of financial records and reporting. Systems & Process Support Maintain general ledger system access for University users. Support accounting operations across various institutional financial systems. Maintain software used for incoming non-student credit card payments, including ticketing, continuing education, and departmental transactions. Grant & Special Fund Accounting Perform accounting and reporting tasks related to public and private grants. Assist in ensuring compliance with grant requirements and financial reporting obligations. International & Auxiliary Accounting Serve as liaison for monthly accounting activities related to Harlaxton College and assist with annual financial statement consolidation. University Support & Reconciliation Review and reconcile University purchasing card transactions. Serve as a liaison to student government representatives and other student organizations regarding financial matters. Perform additional accounting and financial duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Accounting. Proficiency with Microsoft Excel. Knowledge of Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP). Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Strong attention to detail and organizational skills. Self-motivated with the ability to manage multiple responsibilities and deadlines. Preferred Qualifications Working knowledge of ERP systems. [RTFV Job P...staff acct | PDF] Prior accounting experience, preferably in higher education, nonprofit, or public sector environments. Experience with grant accounting and financial reporting. Familiarity with financial reconciliations and fixed asset accounting. Benefits The University of Evansville offers a comprehensive benefits package including: Medical, dental, vision, life, and disability insurance plans. Access to the University's on-site health clinic. [403(b) retirement plan with employer match. Generous vacation and paid holiday benefits. Wellness resources and programs. Full tuition waiver for employees, spouses, and dependent children. Why Join the University of Evansville? The University of Evansville is committed to providing a supportive and collaborative work environment where employees play an important role in advancing the institution's mission. As a Staff Accountant, you will contribute to the University's financial operations while working alongside dedicated professionals who support student success and institutional excellence. How to Apply Interested candidates should complete the online application via the University of Evansville’s employment portal: http://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employmentApp.cfm Legal Statement The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Any form of harassment undermines the mission of the University and negatively impacts the University community as a whole. The University of Evansville participates in the E-Verify program Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3328": {
      "title": "Adjunct Foundation Studio Instructors",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Adjunct Foundation Studio Instructors The Department of Art is seeking adjunct instructors to teach Foundation Studio courses. Potential teaching assignments include Introduction to Studio Art (non-major), Introduction to Art History (non-major), 2D Design, and all levels of Drawing. Requirements: Applicants should have at least a graduate degree (MA or MFA) in Studio Art or a closely related field. Teaching and/or professional studio experience is preferred. The classes are typically held in-person with schedules based on applicant availability and department needs. Application Process: Please complete the application process and submit a current C.V via https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-application-form-faculty.cfm This is an open application for future semesters and program needs. Contact Information: If you have any questions, please contact Todd Matteson at tm8@evansville.edu. Information about the department and our course offerings can be found at https://www.evansville.edu/majors/art/index.cfm Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3228": {
      "title": "Adjunct Mathematics Instructors",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Adjunct Mathematics Instructors Adjunct Mathematics Instructor The University of Evansville Mathematics Department is seeking part-time instructor(s) to teach College Algebra and/or Introductory Statistics courses in Fall 2025. A master’s degree in mathematics or a closely related field is required, and teaching experience is preferred. For non-locals with experience teaching online mathematics or statistics classes, please discuss this in your cover letter. How to Apply: To apply please complete the online application at https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-application-form-faculty.cfm . Please attach a cover letter, CV, and professional references. Considerations of applications will begin immediately. Official academic transcripts will be required at the time of hire. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/709": {
      "title": "Adjunct Nursing Instructors",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Adjunct Nursing Instructors The University is inviting applications for part-time instructors for various clinical courses. This is an on-going position. Minimum qualifications include an MSN with mental health nursing experience. To apply, complete the online application at https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-application-form-faculty.cfm . Attach a single PDF file containing a cover letter, CV, unofficial transcripts and contact information for three references to Katie Thomas at kt149@evansville.edu . Consideration of applications will begin immediately. Official academic transcripts will be required at the time of hire. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3304": {
      "title": "Adjunct Psychology Instructors",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Adjunct Psychology Instructors The Department of Psychology and Behavioral Sciences is seeking adjunct instructors in Psychology to teach PSYC 121: Introduction to Psychology courses and PSYC 259: Abnormal Psychology. Applicants should have at least a graduate degree in Psychology, Social Work, or related field, teaching and/or field experience is preferred. These classes are in-person on M/W/F or T/Th. (based on applicant availability). Please complete the application form and submit an updated c.v. This is an open application for future semesters and program needs. If you have any questions, please contact Dr. Beth Hennon at eh82@evansville.edu Information about the department, including course information can be found at https://www.evansville.edu/majors/psychology/index.cfm Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3303": {
      "title": "Adjunct Sociology Instructors",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Adjunct Sociology Instructors The Department of Psychology and Behavioral Sciences is seeking adjunct instructors in Sociology to teach SOC 105: Introduction to Sociology. Applicants should have at least a graduate degree in Sociology or a related field, teaching and/or field experience is preferred. The classes are in-person on M/W/F or T/Th. (based on applicant availability). Please complete the application process and submit a current c.v. This is an open application for future semesters and program needs. If you have any questions, please contact Dr. Mari Plikuhn at mp168@evansville.edu Information about the department, including course information can be found at https://www.evansville.edu/majors/sociology/ Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3378": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Nurse Anesthesia Program",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Assistant Professor - Nurse Anesthesia Program The University of Evansville invites applications for a motivated, expert clinician-educator to join our esteemed Nurse Anesthesia Program as an Assistant Professor. This position is scheduled to begin on January 1, 2027. In this faculty role, you will work closely with program leadership to teach within a developed curriculum, assess student outcomes, and advise students while ensuring continuous program excellence. Whether you choose a tenure-track path or a clinical faculty path, this position offers a unique balance of teaching, mentorship, scholarly opportunities, and optional clinical practice. Key Responsibilities Didactic Instruction & Course Coordination: Develop, organize, deliver, and assess assigned courses. Manage syllabi, schedules, lecture objectives, and evaluation tools while maintaining expert knowledge in subject matter. Student Advising & Mentorship: Mentor professional-phase nurse anesthesia students throughout their course of study, offering academic, professional, and personal guidance. Record Keeping: Maintain accurate course and student records for assessment, submitting all documentation to the University by established deadlines. Recruitment & Community Outreach: Represent the program to prospective students, families, the University, and the broader community. Committee Service: Actively participate in required programmatic committees as well as College and University-wide committees. Scholarly & Professional Engagement: Engage in ongoing scholarship, professional development, and consulting activities, including attendance at conferences and research initiatives. Required Qualifications Education: Must hold a doctoral degree (DNP, DNAP, or PhD) from an accredited institution recognized by the US Secretary of Education. Certification: Must hold current certification or recertification as a CRNA by the NBCRNA. Industry Awareness: Demonstrated knowledge of environmental and regulatory issues influencing nurse anesthesia practice and education. Perks & Professional Flexibility Tenure-Track Option: Faculty members have the option to pursue a tenure-track appointment. Clinical Practice Opportunity: Faculty in clinical programs have the unique opportunity to maintain active clinical practice by working up to 8 hours per week outside the University in their specialty. Why Join the University of Evansville? At the University of Evansville, our health sciences and graduate nursing programs are committed to rigorous education, interprofessional collaboration, and hands-on clinical excellence. You will join a supportive, mission-driven faculty dedicated to shaping the future of nurse anesthesia in a collaborative academic environment. How to Apply & Timeline Anticipated Start Date: January 1, 2027. Application Process: Interested candidates should complete the online application via the University of Evansville’s employment portal: https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-application-form-faculty.cfm The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, and all federally protected groups/classes. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3318": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Assistant Professor of Physical Therapy Position Overview We are on the lookout for a passionate faculty member to join our thriving Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) Program in the city of Evansville, Indiana. Imagine yourself in a full-time, 10-month position with the possibility of tenure-track, provided you hold an earned terminal degree (PhD, EdD, DSc, HSD, etc.). Our faculty and environment are vibrant because we are passionate about creating the future generation of physical therapy leaders. The requirements for this exciting role include one of two options: 1) a terminal academic degree in neurobiology, physiology, or research methods; or 2) a Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) degree or a DPT combined with an earned post-professional academic doctorate with current expertise in geriatrics, pharmacology, acute care, or cardiopulmonary rehabilitation. If you have a DPT degree, ensure you are eligible for physical therapy licensure in Indiana and bring at least three years of clinical experience. Beyond the classroom, this role extends into student advising, focused scholarship, and service within the department, university, and the broader profession. Your journey with us would begin on August 1, 2026. At the University of Evansville, we champion diversity and operate under a nondiscriminatory policy, embracing individuals of all backgrounds, genders, orientations, and abilities. We encourage minorities and underrepresented groups to seize this opportunity to contribute to our rich tapestry of knowledge. Join us as we make strides in education and be part of a community that values your unique perspective. Bonus points if you appreciate collaborative colleagues, meaningful work, and the occasional Qdoba taco bar. The University of Evansville eagerly awaits your transformative presence. Are you ready to shape the future? Apply now! Responsibilities Include Teaching in assigned DPT content areas Student advising and mentoring Continuing scholarship with student involvement Service to the University, community, and profession Participation in curriculum development and accreditation activities Requirements / Qualifications Required PhD or equivalent terminal degree in a related discipline or DPT with an earned post-professional academic doctorate or DPT with a contemporary expertise Demonstrated expertise relevant to DPT education Preferred Physical therapy licensure or eligibility in Indiana Board certification or advanced clinical training Record of scholarly productivity Higher education teaching experience Other Information Start Date: August 1, 2026 Location: Evansville, Indiana Applications reviewed as received until position filled The University of Evansville offers a generous benefits package to eligible employees, including: Comprehensive Health, Vision, Dental, Group Life, Voluntary Life, and ancillary benefits. Access to our exclusive on-site medical clinic for those enrolled in our Health plan Excellent 403(b) retirement match and a Roth, up to 5% 100% Tuition Remission and Tuition Exchange programs for you, your spouse, and dependents Comprehensive paid holidays Generous sick policy for peace of mind How to Apply Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit application materials via the University of Evansville’s employment portal: https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-application-form-faculty.cfm The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Any form of harassment undermines the mission of the University and negatively impacts the University community as a whole. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3406": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Academic Advisor The University of Evansville invites applications for the position of Academic Advisor. This position plays a critical role in advancing student success, persistence, and degree completion through proactive academic advising, individualized student support, and strategic retention initiatives. The Academic Advisor serves as a key resource for students, particularly undecided students and those experiencing academic challenges. Through advising, academic coaching, outreach efforts, and early intervention strategies, the Academic Advisor helps students navigate their academic journey and overcome barriers to success. This position contributes directly to the University's strategic goal of increasing sophomore-to-junior retention through timely support, engagement, and data-informed student success initiatives. Key Responsibilities The Academic Advisor supports student achievement through advising, coaching, retention efforts, and academic intervention services. Academic Advising & Student Support Advise assigned undecided students and assist in developing academic plans that support timely progress toward degree completion. Meet with students to address scheduling concerns, major and minor exploration, transfer credit questions, academic challenges, and other enrollment-related issues. Assist incoming first-year students prior to SOAR by developing academic plans and supporting course planning and registration. Provide individualized guidance to help students navigate institutional policies, procedures, and academic requirements. Maintain accurate advising records and student documentation. Academic Restoration & Student Success Initiatives Monitor the progress of students participating in the Academic Restoration Program (ARP). Provide timely intervention, follow-up, referrals, and support for students experiencing academic difficulties. Conduct proactive outreach to students identified as needing additional support. Connect students with appropriate campus resources and support services. Academic Coaching Program Coordination Coordinate all aspects of the Academic Coaching Program. Recruit, hire, train, and support academic coaches. Promote participation in academic coaching services among students. Match students with appropriate coaching support based on identified needs. Monitor program utilization and assess program effectiveness. Recommend enhancements and improvements to coaching services based on outcomes and student needs. Retention & Early Alert Initiatives Assist with proactive retention efforts, including targeted outreach campaigns and student success initiatives. Monitor and respond to Purple Post \"Group A\" alerts. Conduct timely follow-up with students identified through early-alert systems and retention initiatives. Identify and address barriers related to academic performance, registration, finances, personal concerns, and other factors affecting persistence. Document student interactions and intervention outcomes. Student Engagement & Education Conduct classroom visits and presentations to promote student engagement with advising and academic support services. Help students understand registration processes, academic planning, and available support resources. Encourage early utilization of advising and academic support services. Assessment & Continuous Improvement Utilize advising data, student interactions, and program outcomes to identify trends and challenges affecting student success. Recommend improvements to advising, coaching, and retention practices. Contribute to institutional efforts designed to improve retention and student persistence. Support the University's strategic goal of increasing sophomore-to-junior retention through proactive advising and intervention strategies. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree. Two to three years of professional experience in academic advising, student success, higher education, enrollment services, or a related field. Strong interpersonal and relationship-building skills. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to advise students and assist with academic planning and problem-solving. Strong organizational, analytical, and follow-through skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities while maintaining attention to detail. Commitment to student success, retention, and inclusive student support. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and campus partners. Preferred Qualifications Experience working with student information systems, advising software, or early-alert platforms. Experience coordinating student success, retention, peer coaching, mentoring, or academic support programs. Familiarity with higher education retention strategies and student success best practices. Experience analyzing student success data and implementing intervention strategies. Knowledge of academic policies, curriculum planning, and enrollment processes. Working Environment The Academic Advisor regularly engages with students, faculty, and staff across the University and serves as a visible advocate for student success. This position requires a collaborative, student-centered approach and the ability to balance proactive outreach efforts with individualized advising support. Suggested Start Date: As soon as possible. Why Join the University of Evansville? The University of Evansville is committed to providing a transformative student experience and fostering a culture of academic success. As an Academic Advisor, you will have a direct impact on students' educational journeys by helping them navigate challenges, achieve their goals, and persist toward graduation. This position offers the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to institutional retention goals while supporting students in a supportive and collaborative campus environment. How to Apply Interested candidates should submit application materials through the University of Evansville employment portal. Legal Statement The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Any form of harassment undermines the mission of the University and negatively impacts the University community as a whole. The University of Evansville participates in the E-Verify program. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3388": {
      "title": "Admissions Processing Specialist",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Admissions Processing Specialist The University of Evansville Office of Admission invites applications for the position of Admissions Processing Specialist. This position plays a critical role in supporting the University's enrollment efforts through the accurate processing of prospective student information and application materials. The successful candidate will be a detail-oriented, service-focused professional who thrives in a collaborative environment while also working independently. This individual will support daily admission operations, maintain data integrity, and contribute to a positive experience for prospective students and their families throughout the recruitment and admission process. Key Responsibilities The Admissions Processing Specialist supports the Office of Admission through data management, communication processes, and operational support. Responsibilities include: Admissions Processing & Data Management Enter and maintain prospective student, applicant, and inquiry data with a high level of accuracy and consistency. Process student leads and application-related information within the University's student information and CRM systems. Monitor and verify data quality while identifying and correcting discrepancies as needed. Maintain accurate records in accordance with institutional policies and best practices. Communication & Correspondence Print, prepare, and process direct mail communications for prospective students and families. Assist with the execution and distribution of admission-related correspondence and communications. Support communication efforts throughout the student recruitment and application process. Operational Support Assist with workflow management and process improvement initiatives within the Office of Admission. Contribute to the development and maintenance of application processing procedures and documentation. Assist with staff training, training materials, and process manuals related to admission operations. Identify opportunities to improve efficiency and effectiveness within admission processes. Collaboration & Customer Service Work collaboratively with admission staff, campus partners, student ambassadors, and other stakeholders. Provide professional and responsive service to prospective students, current students, and families. Maintain positive working relationships across campus departments to support enrollment goals. Participate in special projects and other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent; associate's or bachelor's degree preferred. Strong attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy. Excellent organizational and time-management skills. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities while meeting deadlines. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and standard office technology. Willingness to learn new systems, procedures, and technologies. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in admissions, enrollment management, higher education administration, or a related office environment. Experience with Slate CRM or similar customer relationship management and student information systems. Experience with data entry, records management, and database maintenance. Demonstrated ability to identify process improvements and implement operational efficiencies. Experience developing training materials, procedural manuals, or workflow documentation. Desired Characteristics The ideal candidate will demonstrate: High energy and enthusiasm for supporting student recruitment efforts. A strong customer-service mindset. An organized and efficient work style. The ability to learn quickly and adapt to changing priorities. Initiative in identifying projects and opportunities for improvement. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to build collaborative relationships with colleagues, students, and families. A commitment to accuracy, professionalism, and continuous improvement. Why Join the University of Evansville? The Office of Admission serves as the front door to the University, helping prospective students and families navigate the enrollment process. As an Admissions Processing Specialist, you will play a vital role in supporting recruitment efforts, managing critical student data, and contributing to a welcoming and student-focused experience. You will join a collaborative team dedicated to helping future students begin their journey at the University of Evansville. How to Apply Interested candidates should complete the online application via the University of Evansville’s employment portal: http://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employmentApp.cfm The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. The University is committed to fostering an inclusive environment and is an equal opportunity employer. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3402": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Harlaxton Academic and Faculty Support",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Coordinator of Harlaxton Academic and Faculty Support The University of Evansville invites applications for the position of Coordinator for Harlaxton Academic & Faculty Support. This position provides essential administrative support for the academic operations of Harlaxton College and serves as a key University of Evansville-based resource for faculty coordination, academic scheduling, registration management, academic systems, and related administrative processes. Working under the supervision of the Manager for Enrollment & Program Operations, the Coordinator supports a variety of recurring processes that connect Harlaxton College, University of Evansville offices, visiting faculty, permanent Harlaxton faculty, and students. The successful candidate will play a vital role in ensuring that academic schedules, faculty records, registrations, syllabi, and related administrative systems are maintained accurately, efficiently, and effectively. Key Responsibilities The Coordinator for Harlaxton Academic & Faculty Support assists with a wide range of academic and faculty operations that support the successful delivery of Harlaxton programs. Faculty Coordination Coordinate semester and summer course offerings, faculty information, academic timetables, class schedules, and classroom assignments. Collect, maintain, and track faculty documentation, applications, syllabi, deadlines, and related academic information. Provide ongoing communication, guidance, and administrative support to visiting and permanent faculty. Coordinate and co-host faculty pre-departure information sessions and related orientation activities. Support faculty planning initiatives, including development and administration of the Faculty Ambassador Program. Assist with faculty onboarding workflows and administrative processes. Academic Scheduling & Registration Management Manage student registration processes and enrollment adjustments. Support course enrollment management, including British Studies course balancing and add/drop processes. Coordinate academic scheduling activities to ensure accurate course offerings and classroom assignments. Maintain records and documentation related to course scheduling and registration activities. Work collaboratively with University offices and Harlaxton staff to resolve registration and scheduling issues. Systems & Data Management Build and maintain Harlaxton courses and faculty records within Colleague. Manage and maintain current syllabi within the University syllabus repository. Support Slate administration related to faculty applications, onboarding, and workflow management. Develop and improve automated processes, workflows, and system efficiencies where appropriate. Ensure the accuracy and integrity of academic and faculty records across multiple administrative systems. Administrative Process Improvement Develop and maintain workflows, checklists, templates, process documentation, and training materials. Identify opportunities to improve administrative effectiveness and efficiency. Maintain organized records and documentation that support academic and faculty operations. Assist with special projects and other administrative initiatives as assigned. Financial Processing & Administrative Support Support financial processing related to academic and faculty operations. Assist with tracking and maintaining records associated with departmental budgets and expenditures. Coordinate administrative processes involving multiple stakeholders across both campuses. Provide general operational support for Harlaxton academic programming. Website & Communications Support Assist with maintaining academic and faculty information on University websites and internal resources. Coordinate communication between faculty, staff, and administrative offices. Support dissemination of important academic schedules, deadlines, and program information. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree or an equivalent combination of education and relevant professional experience. Minimum of two years of administrative, academic support, higher education, or related professional experience preferred. Strong organizational and administrative skills with the ability to manage multiple recurring processes and deadlines simultaneously. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Ability to work independently while exercising sound judgment and discretion. Strong technology skills and willingness to learn new systems and platforms. Ability to work effectively with faculty, students, staff, and external academic partners. Ability to coordinate projects involving multiple stakeholders and competing priorities. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in higher education, academic administration, faculty support, or enrollment operations. Experience with Colleague, Slate, or similar student information and customer relationship management systems. Experience managing academic schedules, registration processes, or faculty records. Knowledge of study abroad or international education programs. Experience creating workflows, process documentation, and training materials. Familiarity with website content management systems and academic repositories. Working Environment Part-time position, primarily remote. Academic-year schedule (August through May). Summer hours required during June and July (approximately five hours per week). Typical schedule is Monday through Friday from 8:30 a.m. to 12:30 p.m., or another mutually agreed-upon schedule with the supervisor. Remote work arrangement, with candidates located in the Evansville area strongly preferred as occasional in-person meetings may be required. Position is not eligible for paid holidays, vacation benefits, or other employee benefits. Why Join the University of Evansville? Harlaxton College offers students a distinctive international educational experience rooted in academic excellence and global engagement. The Coordinator for Harlaxton Academic & Faculty Support plays an important role in ensuring the success of academic programs and faculty operations that support students studying at one of the University's most unique and impactful educational sites. This position offers the opportunity to collaborate with faculty, staff, and students across two campuses while contributing to the continued success of Harlaxton programs. How to Apply Interested candidates should submit application materials through the University of Evansville employment portal. Legal Statement The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Any form of harassment undermines the mission of the University and negatively impacts the University community as a whole. The University of Evansville participates in the E-Verify program. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3373": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Distribution Services",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Coordinator, Distribution Services The University of Evansville (UE) is seeking a proactive, organized, and reliable Coordinator, Distribution Services in our campus mailing and receiving operations. This is a critical, hands-on role that keeps our university connected, ensuring the seamless flow of mail, packages, and materials to faculty, staff, and students across campus. If you are a natural leader who enjoys a fast-paced, active environment and takes pride in operational excellence, we invite you to join our Administrative Services team. You will be the point person for all incoming and outgoing logistics, providing leadership to our staff and students while maintaining the high standards our community expects. Key Responsibilities The Coordinator, Distribution Services balances operational leadership with active, daily participation in logistics. Your main duties will include: Team Leadership: Provide daily oversight, training, and supervision for Distribution Services staff and student employees; manage work priorities to ensure all deadlines are met. Logistics & Receiving: Oversee the receipt, tracking, and timely distribution of all campus mail and packages; maintain accurate delivery records. Fiscal & Vendor Management: Monitor postage accounts, manage vendor communications/invoicing, and handle the reconciliation of department expenses. Operational Readiness: Coordinate the maintenance of departmental vehicles, forklifts, and loading dock equipment to ensure all assets are safe and functional. Compliance & Policy: Maintain a deep working knowledge of USPS regulations, carrier requirements, and University policies to ensure full compliance. Hands-On Support: Serve as a backup for Central Receiving and Mail Courier functions, ensuring operations continue smoothly regardless of the daily volume. Required Qualifications Licensure: Must maintain a valid operator’s driver’s license. Technical Skills: Strong working knowledge of computer applications and logistics tracking software. Communication: Exceptional customer service, problem-solving, and interpersonal skills. Organization: Proven ability to multitask, manage time effectively, and adapt to changing priorities in a high-volume environment. Integrity: The ability to exercise discretion and maintain confidentiality when handling university and personal mail/information. Physical Requirements Strength & Agility: Capability to regularly lift and carry up to 50 lbs. Environment: Ability to work outdoors in various weather conditions and move frequently throughout the campus. Why Join the Administrative Services Team at UE? This is not a traditional desk job. Joining the University of Evansville means becoming a key contributor to a collaborative campus community. You will enjoy a dynamic, hands-on work environment where you interact daily with students, faculty, staff, and vendors. If you are looking for a role that keeps you active, challenged, and integral to the daily operations of a premier university, this is the perfect opportunity for you. How to Apply Interested candidates should complete the online application via the University of Evansville’s employment portal: http://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employmentApp.cfm The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3405": {
      "title": "Courier, Receiving/Distribution Services",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Courier, Receiving/Distribution Services The University of Evansville invites applications for the position of Courier, Receiving/Distribution Services. This full-time position is responsible for receiving, tracking, processing, and delivering freight shipments, office supplies, purchase orders, internal supplies, and related materials to campus departments while supporting the daily operations of Distribution Services. The successful candidate will play an important role in ensuring timely and accurate delivery of materials across campus while providing exceptional customer service to faculty, staff, students, and vendors. This position offers a dynamic work environment with responsibilities that span shipping and receiving, inventory management, equipment operation, customer service, and administrative support. Key Responsibilities The Courier supports the University community through efficient distribution, delivery, and inventory operations. Shipping & Receiving Receive, process, track, and deliver freight shipments, office supplies, in-house supplies, and purchase orders to campus departments. Prepare and complete shipping, receiving, inventory, and delivery documentation. Enter and maintain accurate records within departmental systems and databases. Coordinate deliveries and pickups to ensure timely service to campus departments. Distribution & Operations Operate department vehicles and equipment, including delivery vans, forklifts, and pallet jacks, in a safe and efficient manner. Maintain delivery schedules and ensure materials are delivered accurately and professionally. Schedule and assist with routine maintenance and service for department vehicles and equipment. Maintain clean, organized, and safe warehouse, vehicle, and work environments. Inventory Management Monitor inventory levels for office forms, supplies, and other stocked items. Assist with ordering and replenishment processes as needed. Maintain accurate inventory records and tracking systems. Support warehouse organization and inventory control initiatives. Customer Service Provide outstanding customer service to faculty, staff, students, vendors, and campus visitors. Respond to inquiries received through Central Receiving email, telephone, and other communication channels. Assist with sorting, processing, and distribution of campus mail and student packages as needed. Build positive working relationships with campus departments and external vendors. Administrative Support Assist with monthly reports, departmental tracking, and data entry activities. Support journal entries and routine departmental administrative functions. Contribute to operational reporting and process improvement initiatives. Assist with cross-functional responsibilities within Distribution Services as assigned. Required Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Valid U.S. driver's license with an acceptable driving record. Forklift operating experience or the ability to obtain forklift certification within the first six months of employment. Ability to lift and carry up to 50 pounds on a regular basis. Ability to bend, stoop, climb stairs, and perform physically active work throughout the day. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Basic computer proficiency, including email, spreadsheets, and data entry. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Customer-focused attitude with the flexibility to work in a service-oriented environment. Ability to manage multiple priorities independently while working effectively as part of a team. Preferred Qualifications Experience in shipping, receiving, warehouse operations, distribution services, logistics, or a related field. Knowledge of inventory management practices and warehouse procedures. Forklift operator experience or ability to certify within first six months of employment. Working Environment This is a full-time, 12-month hourly staff position scheduled for 40 hours per week. Regular Schedule: Monday through Thursday: 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Friday: 8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. 30-minute lunch period The position requires frequent lifting, carrying, walking, climbing stairs, operating equipment, and working in warehouse, delivery, and campus environments. Why Join the University of Evansville? Distribution Services plays an important role in supporting the University's daily operations. As a Courier, you will help ensure that departments receive the materials and resources they need to serve students and accomplish the University's mission. This position offers a collaborative work environment, meaningful campus impact, and the opportunity to provide exceptional service to the University community. How to Apply Interested candidates should submit application materials through the University of Evansville employment portal. Legal Statement The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Any form of harassment undermines the mission of the University and negatively impacts the University community as a whole. The University of Evansville participates in the E-Verify program. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3396": {
      "title": "Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Maintenance Technician The University of Evansville Facilities Management and Planning department is seeking a skilled and versatile Maintenance Technician to join our campus operations team. This is a full-time, in-person position operating on the first shift, working directly for the University to ensure our academic, residential, and administrative facilities remain safe, functional, and efficient. If you are a hands-on professional who thrives in a multi-trade environment and takes pride in problem-solving and quality workmanship, we invite you to apply for an immediate hire to join our existing team. Key Responsibilities The Maintenance Technician provides comprehensive trade and operational support across campus. Your main duties will include: Building & Systems Maintenance: Complete repairs, construction, and maintenance of university buildings and systems. Respond to work order requests providing carpentry, electrical, plumbing, and HVAC support. Mechanical & Systems Operations: Perform skilled installation, operation, maintenance, modification, and repair of electrical, HVAC, plumbing, and refrigeration control systems. System Monitoring & Troubleshooting: Interpret Energy Management System (EMS) alarms, temperature, and pressure differentials to troubleshoot issues and optimize building performance. Preventive Maintenance: Ensure the proper operation of pumps, engines, motors, and compressors; maintain electronic test equipment and mechanical tools according to operator manuals. Structural & Trade Support: Perform routine carpentry and basic plumbing/electrical repairs based on work orders or oral instructions to update university equipment and materials. Digital Documentation: Accurately track repair costs and labor hours using our mobile CMMS (Computerized Maintenance Management System) app. Collaborative Service: Promote cooperation, trust, and exceptional customer service across our multi-trade environment, and assist with other university duties and events as required. Required Qualifications Education: High School Diploma or equivalent; or any combination of education, training, and experience that provides the necessary knowledge and skills. Licensure: Must possess a valid driver’s license and an acceptable driving record to operate university vehicles and equipment. Communication: Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to build professional relationships and communicate clearly in a service-oriented setting. Physical & Operational Requirements Schedule: Full-time, in-person position operating during the first shift. Strength & Agility: Ability to lift up to 50 lbs, climb stairs/ladders, and perform repetitive motions. Environment: Comfortable working in various conditions, including exposure to hot/cold outdoor temperatures and proximity to hazardous building materials (e.g., solvents, asbestos). Mobility: Frequent walking, standing, bending, twisting, and the ability to operate motorized campus equipment. Why Join the UE Facilities Team? At the University of Evansville, our maintenance staff are the engines that keep our campus running. You will work in a supportive, multi-trade environment where your skills have a direct and visible impact on the student experience. We value craftsmanship, safety, and a proactive \"can-do\" attitude, and we are looking to hire immediately to support our growing team. How to Apply Interested candidates should complete the online application via the University of Evansville’s employment portal: http://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employmentApp.cfm The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, and all federally protected groups/classes. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3390": {
      "title": "Purple Aces Production Technical Director",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Purple Aces Production Technical Director The University of Evansville Athletics Department invites applications for the position of Purple Aces Productions Technical Director. This position plays a critical role in the production and execution of all ESPN+ broadcasts and livestream events associated with the University's Missouri Valley Conference and NCAA Division I athletic programs. The Technical Director serves as the lead producer and director for Purple Aces Productions and is responsible for delivering high-quality broadcasts that meet ESPN and Conference standards. The successful candidate will oversee all aspects of live event production, manage student and part-time production staff, support creative content development, and contribute to classroom instruction within the Department of Communication, when assigned. Key Responsibilities The Technical Director provides leadership for all aspects of livestream and video production operations while ensuring a professional broadcast experience for viewers, partners, and stakeholders. Live Event Production & Broadcast Operations Serve as the lead producer and technical director for all \"The Valley on ESPN\" broadcasts and other assigned livestream events. Direct live broadcasts for Men's Basketball, Women's Basketball, Men's Soccer, Women's Soccer, Volleyball, Baseball, Softball, and other designated events. Ensure all productions meet ESPN, Missouri Valley Conference, NCAA, and University quality standards. Oversee all aspects of event production, including staffing, directing, staging, troubleshooting, script preparation, quality control, and final review. Coordinate and manage event logistics to ensure successful execution of broadcasts. Technical Leadership Direct production staff to ensure high-quality video, audio, graphics, and lighting throughout broadcasts. Ensure consistency, compatibility, and standardization of deliverables for ESPN and other broadcast platforms. Monitor and maintain broadcast equipment, production systems, and technical workflows. Develop and implement best practices for production operations and quality assurance. Staff Recruitment, Training & Supervision Recruit, train, schedule, and supervise student employees and part-time event staff. Develop training programs that prepare students for real-world sports production environments. Mentor and evaluate student crew members while fostering a positive learning environment. Create production manuals, workflows, and operational procedures to support efficient event execution. Content Creation & Creative Services Produce original athletics-related video content for promotional, commercial, social media, and in-game entertainment purposes. Collaborate with athletics administration, marketing, and communications staff to create engaging multimedia content. Support videoboard production and special event presentation initiatives. Assist with creative storytelling efforts that enhance the Purple Aces brand. Innovation & Strategic Development Research emerging trends, technologies, and innovations in sports broadcasting and live event production. Recommend and implement enhancements to improve the fan experience and broadcast quality. Evaluate production workflows and identify opportunities for increased efficiency and effectiveness. Client & Stakeholder Relations Communicate directly with sponsors, clients, coaches, and campus partners regarding production needs and expectations. Ensure sponsored content and promotional elements are executed accurately and professionally. Build positive relationships with internal and external stakeholders while maintaining a high standard of customer service. Teaching & Educational Responsibilities Teach one course per academic term, or six credit hours annually, within the Department of Communication if assigned and qualified. Alternatively, perform an equivalent amount of departmental work if teaching responsibilities are not assigned. Provide hands-on educational opportunities and mentorship to students interested in sports media and production careers. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Communication, Media Production, Broadcasting, Sports Media, Digital Media, or a related field. Professional experience in live event production, broadcast television, sports production, or multimedia content creation. Strong knowledge of video production systems, audio systems, graphics integration, and livestream technologies. Experience directing and producing live broadcasts. Excellent organizational, communication, and leadership skills. Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously while meeting deadlines. Ability to work collaboratively with students, coaches, administrators, sponsors, and campus partners. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in a related field. Experience producing ESPN+, conference network, collegiate athletics, or professional sports broadcasts. Experience teaching or mentoring students in a higher education setting. Proficiency with industry-standard production software and equipment. Experience managing student workers and event-based personnel. Knowledge of NCAA Division I athletics and sports media operations. Experience with videoboard production, replay systems, graphics packages, and broadcast workflow management. Working Environment This position requires frequent evening and weekend work based on athletic competition schedules and special events. Travel may be required on occasion. The successful candidate will work in a fast-paced, collaborative environment supporting multiple NCAA Division I athletic programs and University initiatives. Why Join the University of Evansville? The University of Evansville Athletics Department is committed to providing a first-class experience for student-athletes, fans, and partners. As the leader of Purple Aces Productions, you will play a vital role in showcasing the University's athletic programs through nationally distributed broadcasts while helping develop the next generation of sports media professionals through mentorship and experiential learning. How to Apply Interested candidates should complete the online application via the University of Evansville’s employment portal: http://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employmentApp.cfm Legal Statement The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Any form of harassment undermines the mission of the University and negatively impacts the University community as a whole. The University of Evansville participates in the E-Verify program Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3389": {
      "title": "Security Officer",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Security Officer The University of Evansville invites applications for the position of Security Officer within the Office of Public Safety. This vital role supports the University's commitment to maintaining a safe, secure, and welcoming campus environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. The Security Officer serves as an essential member of the campus community, combining active security presence with communication and customer service responsibilities. The successful candidate will help protect University facilities and resources while providing exceptional support to the campus community. Key Responsibilities The Security Officer supports campus safety initiatives through patrol operations, dispatch functions, emergency response, and community engagement. Dispatch & Communication Operations Serve as a central communication point for campus safety operations. Answer emergency and non-emergency calls for service. Monitor campus alarm, surveillance, and security systems. Dispatch public safety personnel and coordinate communications through radio and telephone systems. Maintain situational awareness and communicate effectively during emergency and routine operations. Campus Security & Patrol Conduct routine foot and vehicle patrols of campus buildings, residence halls, parking lots, and grounds. Identify, report, and address potential safety and security concerns. Monitor facilities for unauthorized access, suspicious activity, and security violations. Ensure campus buildings are secured according to established schedules and procedures. Assist with authorized building access for faculty, staff, students, and approved visitors. Emergency Response Respond promptly to medical emergencies, fire alarms, accidents, and security incidents. Provide assistance and support during crisis situations. Coordinate with local law enforcement, fire departments, and emergency medical personnel as needed. Follow established emergency response procedures and protocols. Community Service & Assistance Provide safety escorts for students, faculty, and staff. Assist community members with vehicle lockouts, jump-starts, and other service requests. Serve as a visible, approachable resource for students, employees, and visitors. Provide directions, information, and assistance to campus guests. Foster positive relationships that support a safe and welcoming campus environment. Documentation & Reporting Prepare accurate and detailed incident reports. Maintain daily activity logs and records of calls for service. Document security incidents, safety concerns, and enforcement actions. Ensure confidentiality and integrity of all records and reports. Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED required. Valid driver's license with an acceptable driving record. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to remain calm, professional, and effective during emergency situations. Basic computer proficiency and the ability to use dispatch, reporting, and security-related software systems. Ability to work effectively as part of a team while also performing duties independently. Strong customer service skills and a commitment to serving a diverse campus community. Demonstrated professionalism, reliability, and strong work ethic. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in campus security, law enforcement, public safety, emergency services, military service, or related fields. Experience operating communications or dispatch equipment. CPR, First Aid, or emergency response certifications. Experience preparing reports and maintaining detailed records. Familiarity with security systems, alarm monitoring, and video surveillance technology. Working Conditions Requires shift work, including evenings, nights, weekends, holidays, and occasional overtime. Position requires extensive walking, standing, climbing stairs, and working in varying weather conditions. May require lifting, carrying, or moving equipment. Must be able to respond quickly to emergencies and campus incidents. Why Join the University of Evansville? The Office of Public Safety plays an important role in protecting and serving the University community. Security Officers are highly visible members of campus who contribute to a positive student experience through safety, service, and professionalism. This position offers the opportunity to make a meaningful impact while working in a collaborative and supportive environment. How to Apply Interested candidates should complete the online application through the University of Evansville employment portal: http://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employmentApp.cfm The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Any form of harassment undermines the mission of the University and negatively impacts the University community as a whole. The University of Evansville participates in the E-Verify program. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3377": {
      "title": "Student Receivables Cashier",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Student Receivables Cashier The University of Evansville (UE) Office of Student Financial Services is seeking a professional, detail-oriented, and customer-focused Student Receivables Cashier to join our team. This role is essential to our mission of providing financial guidance and support to students and their families. If you thrive in a fast-paced environment, have a keen eye for detail, and enjoy both independent and collaborative work, we encourage you to apply! Key Responsibilities The Student Receivables Cashier serves as a primary point of contact for financial transactions and billing inquiries. Your main duties will include: Customer Support: Assist students, families, and the campus community via phone, email, and in person, providing daily guidance on billing and financial aid questions. Payment Processing: Post and reconcile student payments accurately. Support other cashier team responsibilities and work collaboratively to resolve complicated billing issues. Financial Reconciliation: Process non-AR cash reconciliation and prepare bank deposits. Maintain accurate records of all transactions to ensure compliance with university policies. Refunds & Stipends: Manage the processing of student refunds and athletic stipends. Administrative Support: Process and direct incoming mail, monitor calls for quality assurance, and provide immediate feedback to ensure exceptional service levels. Team Collaboration: Work closely with the cashiering staff and the wider SFS team to maintain a seamless experience for the campus community. Required Qualifications Education: High school diploma or GED. Experience: Minimum 1 to 3 years of customer service experience. Skills: Strong written and verbal communication skills with a high level of attention to detail. Technology: Capability to work across multiple technology platforms and handle independent tasks. Attributes: Ability to provide exceptional customer service to a diverse population and manage multiple tasks simultaneously in a team environment. Preferred Qualifications Education: Some college education is preferred. Experience: Prior cashiering experience and general office experience. Technology: Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (specifically Word and Excel) is a plus. Why Join the University of Evansville? The Office of Student Financial Services is at the heart of the student experience, helping families navigate the complexities of university billing and financial aid. In this role, you will be part of a supportive team that values immediate feedback and professional growth while making a tangible difference in the lives of our students. How to Apply Interested candidates should submit a resume, cover letter, and references via the University of Evansville’s employment portal: http://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employmentApp.cfm The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Any form of harassment undermines the mission of the University and negatively impacts the University community as a whole. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3407": {
      "title": "Facilities Specialist",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Facilities Specialist The University of Evansville invites applications for the position of Facility Specialist. This hands-on position plays an essential role in supporting campus operations through event setup and logistics, furniture and equipment maintenance, material handling, painting, and general facilities support. The successful candidate will help ensure that University facilities remain functional, safe, and welcoming for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. This position requires an individual who enjoys a variety of responsibilities, takes pride in quality workmanship, and is committed to providing exceptional service to the campus community. Key Responsibilities The Facility Specialist supports campus operations through event logistics, maintenance activities, painting projects, and general facilities support. Event & Logistics Support Deliver, move, and arrange furniture, fixtures, and equipment (FF&E) for campus events and activities. Set up and remove tables, chairs, staging, and specialized event equipment. Assist with event logistics to ensure spaces are prepared in a timely and professional manner. Support campus departments with event-related transportation and setup needs. Inventory & Equipment Maintenance Receive, clean, inventory, and store furniture and equipment. Assemble, disassemble, and repair furniture as needed. Maintain accurate inventory records and assist with tracking equipment usage and condition. Ensure campus furnishings and equipment remain functional and presentable. Material Handling & Transportation Load, unload, transport, and position materials and equipment throughout campus. Operate hand trucks, pallet jacks, forklifts, airless lifts, and other equipment safely and efficiently. Operate University delivery vehicles as required. Assist with rigging, uncrating, and installation of furniture, equipment, and supplies. Painting & Surface Maintenance Prepare surfaces for painting through cleaning, sanding, patching, and related preparation activities. Perform painting projects on buildings, structures, fixtures, furniture, and equipment. Maintain the appearance and condition of campus facilities through routine touch-up and repair work. Assist with preventative maintenance projects involving painted surfaces. Stage Equipment & Event Resources Maintain, repair, clean, and store stage equipment and event-related materials. Ensure proper security and organization of stage equipment inventories. Assist with the setup and operation of equipment required for campus events and activities. General Maintenance & Trades Support Perform basic carpentry and maintenance tasks, including hanging pictures, whiteboards, bulletin boards, and signage. Assist maintenance technicians and skilled trades personnel with various projects as needed. Support facility improvement and repair initiatives throughout campus. Perform other duties as assigned to support the Facilities Department. Safety & Workplace Practices Safely operate aerial lifts and elevated work platforms up to 65 feet in height. Follow established safety procedures and regulations. Identify and report safety, maintenance, and security concerns. Promote a safe and professional work environment while maintaining compliance with University policies. Required Qualifications Education High school diploma or equivalent. Equivalent combinations of education, training, and experience that provide the required knowledge, skills, and abilities may be considered. Licensure Valid driver's license. Ability to maintain a driving record that meets University requirements for operating University vehicles and equipment. Skills & Abilities Strong interpersonal, communication, and customer service skills. Demonstrated ability to work cooperatively and effectively in a service-oriented environment. Ability to establish positive working relationships with faculty, staff, students, vendors, and visitors. Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Physical Requirements Ability to lift, carry, move, and position furniture, equipment, and materials. Ability to stand, walk, climb, bend, and perform physically demanding work throughout the workday. Ability to work at various heights, including from aerial lifts and elevated platforms. Ability to safely operate material handling and maintenance equipment. Preferred Qualifications Experience with event setup and logistics. Experience operating forklifts, pallet jacks, aerial lifts, or similar equipment. Experience in painting, facility maintenance, carpentry, moving services, or related trades. Knowledge of inventory control and warehouse procedures. Experience working in a facilities, maintenance, construction, or higher education environment. Working Environment This is a full-time, in-person position located on the University of Evansville campus. The position reports to the Facility Specialist Supervisor. Regular work hours are during first shift operations. Occasional evening and weekend overtime may be required to support campus events and operational needs. Work is performed both indoors and outdoors and may involve varying weather conditions, heights, and physical demands. Why Join the University of Evansville? The Facilities Department plays a critical role in supporting the University's educational mission by maintaining safe, functional, and welcoming facilities for the campus community. As a Facility Specialist, you will contribute directly to the success of campus events, facility operations, and the overall student experience while working alongside a dedicated and collaborative team. How to Apply Interested candidates should submit application materials through the University of Evansville employment portal. Legal Statement The University of Evansville expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Any form of harassment undermines the mission of the University and negatively impacts the University community as a whole. The University of Evansville participates in the E-Verify program. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3409": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Finance",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Finance The Schroeder Family School of Business Administration at the University of Evansville invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Finance position beginning August 2027. The School seeks an innovative and student-centered finance scholar who is committed to excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. The successful candidate will contribute to the development of future business leaders through engaging undergraduate instruction, scholarly research, and meaningful community engagement within an AACSB-accredited school. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate finance courses in areas such as Corporate Finance, Investments, Derivatives, Insurance, Financial Planning, and Financial Markets and Institutions. Depending on the candidate's expertise and the needs of the program, additional teaching opportunities may include Portfolio Management, Financial Analytics, Financial Technology, Sustainable Finance, Real Estate, and related areas. Faculty are encouraged to develop innovative courses that reflect emerging developments in finance. The successful candidate will maintain an active scholarly research agenda, including peer-reviewed publications, consistent with the school's mission and AACSB faculty qualification standards. Faculty are expected to cultivate strong relationships with students through advising, mentoring, experiential learning projects, undergraduate research, student organizations, and career development initiatives. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a commitment to applied and engaged learning that connects classroom concepts with real-world business and community challenges. The position provides opportunities for close faculty-student interaction, interdisciplinary collaboration, curriculum innovation, and meaningful engagement with the regional business community. Required Position Criteria An earned Ph.D. in Finance or a closely related field from an accredited institution. ABD candidates who expect to complete their doctoral degree before the appointment date will also be considered. Preference will be given to candidates with doctoral degrees from AACSB-accredited business schools. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching and student mentorship. Demonstrated potential to maintain an active scholarly research agenda and publish in peer-reviewed academic journals in finance or related disciplines. Evidence of effective oral and written communication skills. Commitment to fostering an inclusive learning environment and working with a diverse student population. Screening of applications will begin on December 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Applications must be submitted online at https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-application-form-faculty.cfm. Applications must include a cover letter addressing the position qualifications, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, contact information for at least three professional references, and copies of unofficial graduate transcripts. Applicants must combine all required application materials into a single PDF file and upload it under the ‘Upload Additional Materials’ section of the online application. The University of Evansville is a private university located in Evansville, Indiana, committed to academic excellence, experiential learning, and preparing students for meaningful careers and lives of service. The Schroeder Family School of Business Administration offers a collaborative academic environment that emphasizes innovative teaching, student mentorship, professional preparation, and engagement with the business community. The university expects all members of its community to treat each other with respect and civility. Harassing behaviors directed towards any member of our community will not be tolerated. As part of its commitment to non-discrimination, the University specifically prohibits harassment based on any other characteristics set forth in its nondiscrimination statement as follows: including race, color, gender, gender identity and expression, sexual orientation, creed or religion, national origin, age, disability, veteran status and all federally protected groups/classes. Any form of harassment undermines the mission of the University and negatively impacts the University community as a whole. The University of Evansville participates in the E-Verify program. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    },
    "https://www.evansville.edu/offices/hr/employment-detail/3408": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Physics",
      "description": "Employment Opportunity Detail Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Physics The University of Evansville invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Physics beginning August 1, 2027. The successful candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and student engagement. Primary responsibilities include teaching introductory physics courses for both physics majors and non-majors, upper-level undergraduate physics courses, advising students, and participating in departmental, college, and university service activities. The position also includes leadership and participation in science outreach initiatives that engage K-12 students, community partners, and the broader public in the study of physics and the sciences. We seek candidates with experience and enthusiasm for teaching students from a wide range of academic backgrounds, particularly non-physics majors. Preference will be given to candidates whose expertise complements interdisciplinary areas such as applied mathematics, environmental science, computational physics, data science, or related fields. Opportunities exist for collaboration with programs across the sciences and mathematics. A completed Ph.D. in Physics or a closely related field is required by the start date of the appointment. Prior undergraduate teaching experience is preferred, with demonstrated success in teaching introductory physics courses. Experience in community engagement, science outreach, curriculum development, or interdisciplinary collaboration is highly desirable. Please submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts, a statement of teaching philosophy, and a description of previous outreach, teaching, and interdisciplinary experiences as a single PDF to the Department of Physics, University of Evansville at physics@evansville.edu. Three letters of recommendation should also be sent to physics@evansville.edu. Only electronic submissions will be considered. Applicants should also complete the University of Evansville online faculty application. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The University of Evansville is an independent, comprehensive university recognized for excellence in the liberal arts and sciences as well as professional programs. The University enrolls approximately 2,100 students and is known for its commitment to personalized education, undergraduate research, and global engagement, including Harlaxton College, its residential campus in England. The University of Evansville operates under a non-discriminatory policy with regard to race, color, religion, national origin, sex, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity, or any other status protected by law. We welcome applications from individuals who will contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community. The University participates in the E-Verify program. Return to the list of Employment Opportunities Office Phone 812-488-2943 Office Email hr@evansville.edu Office Location Room 118, Olmsted Administration Hall"
    }
  },
